    {
      "id": "d7npi4c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Montane Forests – Altitudinal Variation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As altitude increases, temperature decreases leading to distinct vegetation belts — from subtropical forests to temperate forests and finally alpine vegetation.",
      "id": "zsdzpsq"
    },
    {
      "id": "jhyi3ro",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Mangrove Forests – Coastal Protection"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Mangroves are salt-tolerant forests found in tidal regions. Their complex root systems protect coastlines from erosion and reduce cyclone damage.",
      "id": "7teq72a"
    },
